      * ZA0510V - VERIFICATION-ONLY variant of src/legacy/qrpgsrc/za0510.rpg
      * (05-04), for verify/part05-qcmdexc-runtime. Not part of the taught
      * curriculum and not referenced by any lesson - exists only so this
      * manifest can force the *PSSR/QCMDEXC/CHGDTAARA path (05-04's own
      * exercise 7) and check its result without hand-editing (and having
      * to hand-revert) the real lesson source during an unattended batch.
      *
      * The ONLY difference from za0510.rpg is the compile-time TABPCD
      * data below: its last entry is 'P09999' instead of the real product
      * code 'P00006', exactly as 05-04's own exercise 7 instructs
      * (docs/part05/05-04-reading-arrays-ds-error.md). Since
      * ZAIKOM's own data is untouched, ZAIKOM's real 'P00006' record now
      * has no matching TABPCD entry when read, so LOKUP fails, EXSR
      * *PSSR fires, and *PSSR's CHGDTAARA writes 'ZA0510 ERROR' to *LDA
      * bytes 1-20 - the same evidence 05-04's own exercise asks students
      * to check by hand with DSPDTAARA. All F/E/I/C/O specs below are
      * otherwise byte-for-byte identical to za0510.rpg; see that file's
      * own header for the full design rationale and citations.
     H
     FZAIKOM  IP  E           K        DISK
     F                                              KINFDS ZAINF
     F                                              KINFSR *PSSR
     FQSYSPRT O   F     132            PRINTER
     E                    TABPCD  6   6  6
     E                    TABPRI  6   6  1 0
     E                    SQ          3  7 0
     IZAIKOR
     I              ZASHO                           ZKSHO
     I              ZASU                            ZKSU
     I/COPY FLDREFR
     ICMDDS       DS                             57
     I                                        1   7 C1
     I                                        8  14 C2
     I                                       15  21 C3
     I                                       22  28 C4
     I                                       29  35 C5
     I                                       36  42 C6
     I                                       43  49 C7
     I                                       50  56 C8
     I                                       57  57 C9
     IPSDS       SDS
     I                                       11  150STATUS
     I                                       29  36 RTN
     IZAINF       DS
     I                                       11  150FSTAT
     I                                       22  29 FRTN
     IPRIDS       DS                             21
     I                                        1   70PQ1
     I                                        8  140PQ2
     I                                       15  210PQ3
      * -- detail: one cycle per ZAIKOM record --
     C                     ADD  ZKSU      GQTY    90
     C                     SETOF                     80
     C           ZKSHO     LOKUPTABPCD    TABPRI         80
     C  N80                EXSR *PSSR
     C   80                Z-ADDTABPRI    PRI     10
     C   80                ADD  ZKSU      SQ,PRI
      * -- LR: cross-foot the array against the independent total --
     CLR                   XFOOTSQ        XQTY    90
     CLR         XQTY      COMP GQTY                     93
     CLR                   Z-ADDSQ,1      PQ1
     CLR                   Z-ADDSQ,2      PQ2
     CLR                   Z-ADDSQ,3      PQ3
     CLR                   EXCPT
      * -- subroutines --
      * *PSSR: fatal LOKUP-miss (explicit EXSR) and, program-wide,
      * RPG's default error/exception handler (see header note 8).
     CSR         *PSSR     BEGSR
      * build the QCMDEXC command text into CMDDS (see header note 9)
     C                     MOVEL'CHGDTAA' C1
     C                     MOVEL'RA DTAA' C2
     C                     MOVEL'RA(*LDA' C3
     C                     MOVEL' (1 20)' C4
     C                     MOVEL') VALUE' C5
     C                     MOVEL'(''ZA051'C6
     C                     MOVEL'0 ERROR' C7
     C                     MOVEL''')     'C8
     C                     MOVEL' '       C9
     C                     Z-ADD57        CMDLEN 155
     C                     CALL 'QCMDEXC'              85
     C                     PARM           CMDDS
     C                     PARM           CMDLEN
     CSR                   ENDSR'*CANCL'
     OQSYSPRT E
     O                         PQ1        9
     O                         PQ2       18
     O                         PQ3       27
     O                         GQTY      38
     O                         XQTY      49
     O                 93                55 'OK'
     O                N93                65 'MISMATCH'
**
P00001P00002P00003P00004P00005P09999
**
112233
